WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:14.160
The bun's position helps set the overall mood and compensate for figure-related concerns of the wedding parent.

2
00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:24.168
· Low bun (down-up): Sits near the neckline for an elegant, refined look — the most popular trend among wedding parents today.

3
00:00:24.504 --> 00:00:35.640
· Mid bun (middle-up): Sits at the middle of the back of the head, opening up the neckline when a short neck makes a low bun touch the hanbok collar and look stuffy.

4
00:00:35.976 --> 00:00:42.552
It also suits wedding parents with a youthful sense who want a light, lively image.

5
00:00:42.888 --> 00:00:51.456
· High bun (high-up): Piled up near the crown for a bold, eye-catching look like a party or stage style.

6
00:00:51.792 --> 00:01:04.128
It's recommended for those wanting to appear taller or who enjoy a bold look, but since it can miss the refined image, artists these days use it sparingly and with great care.
